    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Martin O'Connor Estate Agents are delighted to present this exceptional detached waterfront residence 'Lakeside', Ballinakill, Lettermullen, Co. Galway, occupying a peaceful position on the shores of Ballinakill Lough in the heart of Connemara. Enjoying direct frontage onto the lough, together with a private slipway and uninterrupted views across the water, this beautifully maintained home offers a rare opportunity to acquire a distinctive property in one of the West of Ireland's most scenic coastal locations.Extending to approximately 154.3 sq.m. (1,661 sq.ft.), the property has been thoughtfully designed to maximise natural light and take full advantage of its unique surroundings. Beautifully cared for the home offers spacious and well-balanced accommodation throughout. Without doubt, the standout feature of the property is the impressive sunroom, where expansive glazing perfectly frames the peaceful outlook across Ballinakill Lough. Flooded with natural light throughout the day, it provides an exceptional space to relax, entertain or simply enjoy the ever-changing views throughout the seasons.The accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hall, spacious living room, open-plan kitchen and dining area, family bathroom and a generous ground floor double bedroom. At first-floor level there are three further double bedrooms, including a principal bedroom with en suite, together with a well-appointed family bathroom, making the property ideally suited to both family living and those seeking a spacious coastal retreat.Outside, the property is approached through gated entrances onto a spacious tarmac driveway providing excellent parking. Traditional Connemara stone boundary walls, mature gardens and well-maintained grounds create an attractive and private setting around the home. There are three charming stone built outbuildings which further enhances the property's character while providing valuable storage. A private slipway provides direct access to Ballinakill Lough, offering the opportunity to enjoy boating, kayaking, paddle boarding and fishing from your own doorstep.Located in the heart of the Gaeltacht, Lettermullen is renowned for its spectacular coastline, sheltered bays, sandy beaches and rich Irish-speaking heritage. The property is approximately 5.8 km from Lettermore Village and 17.8 km from Carraroe, where a range of shops, cafés, schools and everyday amenities are available. The surrounding area offers an excellent choice of outdoor pursuits, including boating, kayaking, fishing, coastal walks and golf at the nearby Connemara Isles Golf Club. The Seaweed Centre (Ionad na Feamainne), offering seaweed baths, wellness experiences and water-based activities, is also close by, while the surrounding South Connemara coastline and the Wild Atlantic Way provide endless opportunities to explore one of Ireland's most beautiful regions.Whether as a permanent family home, a holiday retreat or a peaceful place to escape, 'Lakeside' offers a wonderful combination of quality accommodation, direct waterfront access and the timeless beauty of Connemara. Properties enjoying lakeside frontage rarely come to the market, making this a unique opportunity to acquire a truly special home in an exceptional coastal setting.To arrange your viewing of this wonderful home please call DNG Martin O'Connor Estate Agents on (091) 866708."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Porch - \nA bright and welcoming entrance hall with tiled flooring and a glazed front door creating an inviting first impression, while providing access to the main living accommodation.\n\nLiving Room - \nA spacious and comfortable reception room featuring a charming open fireplace set within a feature surround, windows overlooking the front of the property, creating a warm and welcoming space for everyday living. Doors to;\n\nBedroom 1 (Ground Floor) - \nA generous double bedroom located on the ground floor, ideal for guests, multi-generational living or use as a home office.\n\nKitchen / Dining Room - \nThe open-plan kitchen and dining area forms the heart of the home and is fitted with an excellent range of solid timber wall and floor units, generous worktop space, integrated appliances and a dedicated space with plumbing for a washing machine. The dining area comfortably accommodates a family-sized table and enjoys direct access to the adjoining sunroom.\n\nSunroom - \nThe standout feature of the property, this exceptional sunroom enjoys uninterrupted views across Ballinakill Lough through expansive glazing. Flooded with natural light throughout the day, it provides a wonderful space to relax and take in the ever-changing lakeside scenery. French doors from the kitchen and dining area create a seamless connection between the two spaces, making it ideal for both everyday living and entertaining.\n\nShower Room - \nFully tiled and fitted with a shower, WC and wash hand basin.\n\nFirst Floor Landing - \nA bright and spacious landing providing access to the first-floor accommodation and useful built-in storage.\n\nPrincipal Bedroom - \nAn exceptionally spacious principal bedroom overlooking Ballinakill Lough, complete with extensive fitted wardrobes, integrated dressing area and a well-appointed en suite shower room.\n\nEn Suite - \nFully tiled and fitted with a shower, WC and wash hand basin.\n\nBedroom 3 - \nA generous double bedroom with fitted carpet and excellent natural light.\n\nFamily Bathroom - \nA spacious family bathroom fitted with a corner bath, WC and wash hand basin, finished with fully tiled walls and flooring.\n\nBedroom 4 - \nAnother spacious double bedroom with fitted carpet, enjoying views of the surrounding countryside.\n\nDetached Stone Outbuilding 1 - \n\n\nStone Outbuilding 2 - \n\n\nStone Outbuilding 3 - \n\n\n"
